title: The Saxon Election
subtitle: Saxony elects a new Landtag.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 11
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
var r = RG.election('saxony', {
    base: {spd: 40, kpd: 10, dnvp: 19, dvp: 19, ddp: 8},
    size: 96,
    kpdShare: 10.5,
    bonus: (Q.e22_reunification == 1 ? 1 : 0) + (Q.e22_inflation_line == 1 ? 1 : 0)
});
Q.e22_sax_spd = r.seats.spd || 0;
Q.e22_sax_majority = Q.landtag_saxony_left_majority;
Q.e22_sax_stood = Q.election_kpd_share > 0 ? 1 : 0;
Q.e22_sax_gain = Q.election_kpd_seats - 10;
if (Q.e22_sax_stood) {
    Q.district_saxony_members *= 1 + Math.max(0, Q.election_kpd_share - 6) / 100;
}
RG.news(Q.e22_sax_majority ? 'Saxony: a majority for the workers\' parties' : 'Saxony: no majority for the workers\' parties', 3);
!}

= The Saxon Election

On 5 November Saxony votes. [? if e22_sax_stood = 1 : The party wins [+ election_kpd_share_display +] per cent and [+ election_kpd_seats +] seats, ?][? if e22_sax_stood = 0 : The party stands no candidates, ?] and the SPD [+ e22_sax_spd +]. [? if e22_sax_majority = 1 : Together the two workers' parties have a majority of the ninety-six seats. ?][? if e22_sax_majority = 0 : The workers' parties are short of a majority. ?] [? if e22_sax_gain >= 3 : It is the party's best result anywhere in Germany. ?]

The Saxon SPD is the most left-wing in the country, and many of its members would rather govern with us than with the Democrats. Its leaders want our votes for a Social Democratic government, and ask our price.

- @tolerate: Support an SPD government, on conditions.
- @ministers: Ask for seats in the government.
- @refuse: No support for Social Democratic ministers.

@tolerate
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Control committees with legal standing, and an amnesty. Saxony becomes our showcase.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids supporting a Social Democratic government.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.e22_saxon_toleration = 1;
RG.district('saxony', {loyalty: 6, militancy: 2});
Q.spd_relation += 5;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The SPD accepts most of our conditions, on paper. A Social Democratic minority government takes office in Dresden with our votes.

@ministers
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Communist ministers a year early. Berlin will be alarmed.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2 and spd_relation >= 35 and e22_sax_majority = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Saxon SPD will not take communist ministers without a majority and more trust.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.e22_saxon_toleration = 3;
Q.saxony_government = 1;
RG.ledger('Communist ministers entered the Saxon government in the autumn of 1922.', 'e22_sax_ministers');
RG.news('Two communists join the Saxon cabinet', 2);
RG.district('saxony', {loyalty: 8, repression: 5});
RG.ecci('radek', 6);
Q.lean_unionist += 3;
!}

After a month of talks two communists take seats in the Saxon cabinet, for labour and for food supply. The Reichswehr commander in Dresden asks Berlin for instructions.

@refuse
subtitle: The SPD governs with the Democrats and blames us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_saxon_toleration = 2;
RG.district('saxony', {loyalty: -6});
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Our deputies vote against every candidate for Minister-President. The SPD forms a government with the Democrats, and its members ask ours what they are for.
